### Student Course Enrollment API (SET B) - Manual Test Suite
### Student: Soumya Verma | Section: CSE 36
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 0. Welcome / Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 1. GET all enrollments (HTTP 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments

### 2. GET low-attendance enrollments (attendance < 75) (HTTP 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/low-attendance

### 3. Filter enrollments by semester (HTTP 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/filter?semester=3

### 4. Filter enrollments by non-matching semester (returns [] HTTP 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/filter?semester=8

### 5. GET enrollment by valid ID (HTTP 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/601

### 6. GET enrollment by non-existent ID (HTTP 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/999

### 7. POST a new enrollment (HTTP 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "Ishita Rao",
  "courseCode": "CS315",
  "courseName": "Operating Systems",
  "semester": 3,
  "attendance": 88
}

### 8. POST with invalid attendance (> 100) (HTTP 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "Invalid Attendance",
  "courseCode": "CS320",
  "courseName": "Compiler Design",
  "semester": 3,
  "attendance": 120
}

### 9. POST with invalid semester (< 1) (HTTP 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "Invalid Semester",
  "courseCode": "CS320",
  "courseName": "Compiler Design",
  "semester": -2,
  "attendance": 75
}

### 10. PUT / update existing enrollment (HTTP 200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/601
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "Aarav Gupta",
  "courseCode": "CS301",
  "courseName": "Data Structures",
  "semester": 4,
  "attendance": 85
}

### 11. PUT / update non-existent enrollment (HTTP 404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "Ghost Student",
  "courseCode": "CS399",
  "courseName": "Unknown",
  "semester": 1,
  "attendance": 50
}

### 12. DELETE enrollment by valid ID (HTTP 200)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/602

### 13. DELETE enrollment with non-existent ID (HTTP 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/999
